More than half of Brazilians are overweight and have an associated comorbidity. Around 20% of Brazilians are already in the obesity range. These medications are commonly known as weight-loss pens. The medication is like a kick-start. The treatment is much more complex than that. Obesity is a chronic disease, like diabetes or hypertension. Even after losing weight, you will not be cured and may regain weight at any time. The assessment of which medication is most appropriate for your case must be individualized and performed by a physician. Improper use without medical guidance can cause adverse effects. People who seek treatment on their own may experience unpleasant side effects, drug interactions, excessive loss of muscle mass known as sarcopenia, brittle nails, malnutrition, and even pancreatic toxicity. The goal is not to help you lose a few pounds for aesthetic reasons, the goal is to restore health and quality of life.